message: "If you use this board, its data or its audit trail, please cite it as below."
title: "Lens by Level: seven ways of looking at a language model, graded by evidence across four levels of description"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Siener
    given-names: Wolfram
date-released: 2026-11-06
version: "9.2"
url: "https://wsiener.dev/lens-by-level/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/wolframs/lens-by-level"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - language models
  - AI welfare
  - interpretability
  - levels of description
  - evidence synthesis
abstract: >-
  An evidence-graded board of 28 cells: seven lenses (mechanistic interpretation,
  behaviour, self-report, dynamics, hedonic theory, preference theory, relation)
  against four levels of a language model (checkpoint, one conversation, one turn,
  one forward pass), with persona as a cross-cutting marker. Every cell carries a
  source tag and an evidence tier; every source carries the level of verification
  reached. Built with Claude (Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5) and checked by an external
  GPT-6 Astra audit, with the full audit trail.
